#X obj 675 8 seq.bangs;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 271 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A bang event sequencer: iterates over a list of durations
and outputs a bang after each duration has elapsed. The pattern is
given in beat duration units (relative to the beat time @t) \, and
each value determines how many beats to wait before the next bang.
Playback can be looped with @r \, reversed with @mode dec or @mode
tri \, and subdivided with @div.;
#X text 240 199 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 224 • Rhythmic triggers for drum synthesis — driving percussive
voices or samplers with a precise rhythmic pattern \, where each bang
corresponds to a drum hit.;
#X text 250 279 • Algorithmic rhythm generation — combining different
patterns \, repeat counts and directions to build evolving rhythmic
structures for generative music.;
